      "updated": 1792849714034,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Transparent scalability: because blocks never wait for\neach other, the same kernel runs unchanged on\nany GPU, which simply executes as many blocks\nat a time as it has room for; more SMs means\nfaster, never different.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
